592186521754 1077 "III" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521754 1078 #edb/ref 17592186521823 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521754 1079 #uuid "0b48a7c4-4358-56a2-b9e1-abd8e70b08cb" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521775 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521755 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521837 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521755 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521755 1077 "V" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521755 1078 #edb/ref 17592186521775 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521755 1079 #uuid "0b9b35e0-eec0-5034-8f33-49c3fb288348" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521756 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521774 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521756 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521756 1071 "At which point on the curve $8 x y + 4 y^{2}=- 4 x^{2} + 2 y + 2$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521756 1072 #uuid "0e539d3d-4951-53af-94a7-c8aeb37adea8" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521756 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 4 y^{2}&=- 4 x^{2} + 2 y + 2\\\\4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 2&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 2$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 2)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 2)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 8 y - 2)\\,i-(8 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\- 8 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=-x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(x+(-x))^{2}-2(-x)-(2)&=0\\\\2x-(2)&=0\\\\2x&=2\\\\x&=1\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding point is $(1,-1)$." 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521757 1080 "$(12,-12)$ only" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521757 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521757 1083 #uuid "0fca5786-6f95-5edc-89d7-025c97273124" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521747 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521755 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521789 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521839 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521850 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521860 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1071 "At which points on the curve $8 x y + 2 y^{2}=16 x^{2} + 432$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-3,-12)$\n- **II.** $(0,12)$\n- **III.** $(\\frac{3}{2},12)$\n- **IV.** $(3,0)$\n- **V.** $(3,6)$\n- **VI.** $(3,12)$" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1072 #uuid "10aa9a22-24d9-5578-9f7c-cc0b57f6bc72" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521758 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 2 y^{2}&=16 x^{2} + 432\\\\- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 4 y)\\,i-(- 32 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\32 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=4x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=4x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}2(4x)^{2}+8x(4x)-16x^{2}-432&=0\\\\48x^{2}-432&=0\\\\x^{2}&=9\\\\x&=\\pm 3\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(3,12)$ and $(-3,-12)$." 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521759 1080 "true" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521759 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521759 1083 #uuid "113382ea-65ed-55c1-ac18-b7478229c5ab" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521760 1080 "true" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521760 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521760 1083 #uuid "115aa2f4-a593-5d77-a880-a7ebe30e68ff" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521763 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521793 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521817 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521828 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521848 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521859 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1071 "At which points on the curve $4 x y + y^{2}=4 x^{2} + 8$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,-2)$\n- **II.** $(0,2)$\n- **III.** $(\\frac{1}{2},2)$\n- **IV.** $(1,0)$\n- **V.** $(1,1)$\n- **VI.** $(1,2)$" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1072 #uuid "138b2fa1-5696-5cfb-b4c1-4b8eecec9f34" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521761 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4 x y + y^{2}&=4 x^{2} + 8\\\\- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + y^{2} - 8&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + y^{2} - 8$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + y^{2} - 8)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + y^{2} - 8)\\,j\\\\&=(4 x + 2 y)\\,i-(- 8 x + 4 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\8 x - 4 y&=0\\\\y&=2x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=2x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}1(2x)^{2}+4x(2x)-4x^{2}-8&=0\\\\8x^{2}-8&=0\\\\x^{2}&=1\\\\x&=\\pm 1\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(1,2)$ and $(-1,-2)$." 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521762 1080 "true" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521762 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521762 1083 #uuid "1582ef11-2a8f-56b8-be1e-533ad686623d" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521835 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521867 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521763 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521763 1077 "III" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521763 1078 #edb/ref 17592186521867 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521763 1079 #uuid "15959162-8202-56a1-a0f2-83319529d308" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521764 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521769 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [