 17592186521872 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521800 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521800 1071 "At which points on the curve $8 x y + 3 y^{2}=16 x^{2} + 1024$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-4,-16)$\n- **II.** $(0,16)$\n- **III.** $(2,16)$\n- **IV.** $(4,0)$\n- **V.** $(4,8)$\n- **VI.** $(4,16)$" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521800 1072 #uuid "5284e034-941a-5de0-a7ad-3718d5b22f4c" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521800 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 3 y^{2}&=16 x^{2} + 1024\\\\- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 1024&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 1024$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 1024)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 1024)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 6 y)\\,i-(- 32 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\32 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=4x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=4x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}3(4x)^{2}+8x(4x)-16x^{2}-1024&=0\\\\64x^{2}-1024&=0\\\\x^{2}&=16\\\\x&=\\pm 4\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(4,16)$ and $(-4,-16)$." 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521801 1080 "$(6,6)$ only" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521801 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521801 1083 #uuid "5564689e-d3ce-5a9f-a719-7eb39d492591" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521802 1080 "false" 13194139535598 17592186045443