2186045443 true] [17592186521870 1072 #uuid "f0a0a0dc-dc0e-505f-ae57-9fc7b81e15fb" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521870 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4 x y + 2 y^{2}&=4 x^{2} + 48\\\\- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48)\\,j\\\\&=(4 x + 4 y)\\,i-(- 8 x + 4 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\8 x - 4 y&=0\\\\y&=2x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=2x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}2(2x)^{2}+4x(2x)-4x^{2}-48&=0\\\\12x^{2}-48&=0\\\\x^{2}&=4\\\\x&=\\pm 2\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(2,4)$ and $(-2,-4)$." 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521871 1080 "false" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521871 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521871 1083 #uuid "f122121f-13ed-5d40-84a7-05ee73afda8c" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521872 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521791 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521872 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521852 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521872 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521872 1077 "IV" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521872 1078 #edb/ref 17592186521852 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521872 1079 #uuid "f1266a7c-b2e9-54bd-aeaa-5ab051911a08" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521873 1080 "true" 13194139535598 17592186045443 true] [17592186521873 1082 #edb/ref 175